%%{init: {"theme": "default", "sequence": {"wrap": true, "noteAlign": "left", "noteMargin": 12, "actorMargin": 80, "messageMargin": 45}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    participant vLLM as vLLM Engine<br/>(GPU Node)
    participant CE as LMCache Engine<br/>(initiator, Architecture A)
    participant SM as StorageManager
    participant L1 as LocalCPUBackend<br/>(L1 DRAM)
    participant TX as WAL + key→LBA map<br/>(initiator-side)
    participant RB as RawBlockL2Adapter<br/>(io_uring / O_DIRECT)
    participant K_INIT as Initiator kernel<br/>nvme_rdma
    participant K_TGT as Target kernel<br/>nvmet_rdma
    participant JBOF as NVMe JBOF<br/>(remote namespace)
    participant GPU as GPU Connector<br/>(DMA to HBM)

    Note over vLLM,JBOF: Architecture A — initiator-owned + remote NVMe-oF L2.<br/>All cache semantics (hash, admission, allocator, WAL, map, checksum verify) live on the initiator.<br/>Target runs standard Linux nvmet + nvmet_rdma and the SSD block layer — no LMCache agent.
    Note over K_INIT,K_TGT: WAL only<br/>COW deferred to Future Work<br/>For NVMe Write target performs RDMA Read from initiator buffer<br/>For NVMe Read target performs RDMA Write to initiator buffer<br/>Transport execution only<br/>No target cache admission or scheduling

    Note over vLLM,JBOF: === RETRIEVE (Cache Lookup) ===

    vLLM->>CE: retrieve(tokens)
    CE->>CE: TokenDatabase: hash tokens → chunk keys (BLAKE3)
    CE->>SM: batched_contains(keys)
    SM->>L1: batched_contains(keys, exclude_pending=true)

    Note over SM,L1: L1 entries in PENDING state (not yet map-published) are<br/>invisible to batched_contains and get. They become visible atomically<br/>with map publication in the STORE flow below.

    alt L1 HIT (page in DRAM)
        L1-->>SM: hit_chunks = N
        SM-->>CE: block_mapping: {LocalCPUBackend: keys}
        CE->>L1: get(keys)
        L1-->>CE: MemoryObj (pinned DRAM buffer)
        CE->>GPU: load → DMA to GPU HBM
        GPU-->>vLLM: KV in HBM, resume inference
    else L1 MISS → check L2 map
        L1-->>SM: hit_chunks = 0
        SM->>TX: lookup(keys) → LBA extents + checksum ref
        alt L2 HIT (key present in initiator map)
            TX-->>SM: LBAs + checksum refs
            SM->>RB: submit_load_task(LBAs, dst_buffers)
            RB->>K_INIT: io_uring submit (O_DIRECT read, 256KB)
            K_INIT->>K_TGT: NVMe Read command + initiator SGL
            K_TGT->>JBOF: block-layer read
            JBOF-->>K_TGT: block data
            K_TGT->>RB: RDMA Write payload into initiator MR
            K_TGT-->>K_INIT: NVMe completion
            K_INIT-->>RB: completion → data in registered DRAM
            RB->>RB: recompute BLAKE3, compare to committed digest
            alt VALIDATE OK
                RB-->>CE: load complete
                CE->>L1: promote to L1 (optional)
                CE->>GPU: load → DMA to GPU HBM
                GPU-->>vLLM: KV in HBM, resume inference
            else VALIDATE FAIL
                RB->>TX: mark key stale / discard map entry
                RB-->>CE: load failed (integrity)
                CE-->>vLLM: miss (recompute)
            end
        else L2 MISS (no map entry)
            TX-->>SM: not present
            SM-->>CE: total_hit_chunks = 0
            CE-->>vLLM: miss mask (recompute these tokens)
        end
    end

    Note over vLLM,JBOF: === STORE (WAL Durable Commit) ===

    vLLM->>CE: store(tokens, kv_tensors)
    CE->>GPU: GPU HBM → DMA to host DRAM
    CE->>CE: hash tokens → chunk keys, compute per-page BLAKE3 digest D
    CE->>CE: assign gen (=1 for first-write, =current_gen+1 for overwrite)
    CE->>CE: run key+digest idempotency check
    Note over CE,SM: Appendix A.5 idempotency (per key). absent → proceed at gen=1. PENDING match same digest → join or retryable. PENDING match different digest → busy/retryable. VISIBLE match → no-op ACK. VISIBLE differ → admit as overwrite at gen+1.
    CE->>SM: put(keys, memory_objs, digests, gen)
    SM->>L1: put(keys, data, state=PENDING) → pinned in DRAM, NOT lookup-visible

    Note over SM,TX: Initiator-side durable commit begins here.<br/>L1 buffer holds data but stays PENDING until step 4c succeeds.<br/>Concurrent retrieve cannot see PENDING entries.

    SM->>TX: 1. append intent { key, gen, LBA_range, D, INTENT } to WAL
    TX->>K_INIT: submit WAL-intent write
    K_INIT->>K_TGT: NVMe Write command + WAL-intent SGL
    K_TGT->>TX: RDMA Read WAL intent from initiator MR
    K_TGT->>JBOF: block-layer write
    JBOF-->>K_TGT: completion
    K_TGT-->>K_INIT: completion
    TX->>K_INIT: NVMe FLUSH intent log
    K_INIT->>K_TGT: NVMe FLUSH
    K_TGT->>JBOF: block-layer flush
    JBOF-->>K_TGT: completion
    K_TGT-->>K_INIT: completion
    K_INIT-->>TX: flush returns

    SM->>RB: 2. submit_store_task(LBA_range, data, FUA)
    RB->>K_INIT: io_uring submit (O_DIRECT write with FUA, 256KB)
    K_INIT->>K_TGT: NVMe Write command + payload SGL (FUA)
    K_TGT->>RB: RDMA Read payload from initiator MR
    K_TGT->>JBOF: block-layer write, FUA → durable payload
    JBOF-->>K_TGT: completion
    K_TGT-->>K_INIT: completion
    K_INIT-->>RB: completion

    RB->>TX: 3. write checksum record (D, LBA_range) with FUA
    TX->>K_INIT: submit checksum write with FUA
    K_INIT->>K_TGT: NVMe Write command + checksum SGL (FUA)
    K_TGT->>TX: RDMA Read checksum from initiator MR
    K_TGT->>JBOF: block-layer write, FUA → durable checksum
    JBOF-->>K_TGT: completion
    K_TGT-->>K_INIT: completion

    Note over TX,K_TGT: Step 4 is the durable-commit + atomic-publish + supersede boundary.<br/>4a = media-durability of new gen. 4b/4c = in-memory publish. 4d = quiesce prior-gen readers. 4e = durable RELEASED of prior gen (overwrite only).<br/>c5 window = anywhere from 4a return through 4e — same on-media state after restart.

    TX->>TX: 4a. append WAL COMMITTED record { key, gen, LBA_range, D, COMMITTED }
    TX->>K_INIT: submit WAL-COMMITTED-record write
    K_INIT->>K_TGT: NVMe Write command + commit-record SGL
    K_TGT->>TX: RDMA Read commit record from initiator MR
    K_TGT->>JBOF: block-layer write
    JBOF-->>K_TGT: completion
    K_TGT-->>K_INIT: completion
    TX->>K_INIT: NVMe FLUSH commit record
    K_INIT->>K_TGT: NVMe FLUSH
    K_TGT->>JBOF: block-layer flush
    JBOF-->>K_TGT: completion
    K_TGT-->>K_INIT: completion
    K_INIT-->>TX: flush returns [c5 window begins — new gen durable on media]

    TX->>TX: 4b. publish key→LBA map entry at new gen (atomic w/ 4c)
    TX->>L1: 4c. flip L1 state PENDING → VISIBLE at new gen (atomic w/ 4b)
    Note over TX,L1: After 4c, no new reader can resolve key to prior gen.

    alt overwrite (prior gen existed)
        TX->>TX: 4d. quiesce readers of prior gen (epoch / RCU drain)
        TX->>TX: 4e. append WAL RELEASED record { key, prior_gen, LBA_range', D', RELEASED }
        TX->>K_INIT: submit WAL-RELEASED-record write + FLUSH
        K_INIT->>K_TGT: NVMe Write + FLUSH commands
        K_TGT->>JBOF: block-layer write + flush
        JBOF-->>K_TGT: completions
        K_TGT-->>K_INIT: completions
        K_INIT-->>TX: RELEASED flush returns [c5 window ends — prior extent GC-eligible]
    else first-write (no prior gen)
        Note over TX,K_INIT: skip 4d/4e — no reader quiesce, no RELEASED to write
    end

    TX-->>SM: 4f. return terminal ACK
    SM-->>CE: store ACK (terminal, cache-visible)

    Note over SM,L1: If any step fails before 4a's flush returns, the PENDING L1 entry is dropped on restart — it was never lookup-visible.<br/>If the crash lands anywhere in the c5 window (4a → 4e), WAL replay reconstructs the new value at gen exactly once. For overwrites, replay emits a synthetic RELEASED for the prior gen.

    Note over vLLM,JBOF: === RECOVERY (restart / nvme reconnect) ===

    CE->>TX: replay WAL
    TX->>K_INIT: read intent + commit log + checksum region
    K_INIT->>K_TGT: NVMe Read commands + initiator SGLs
    K_TGT->>JBOF: block-layer reads
    JBOF-->>K_TGT: log + checksum blocks
    K_TGT->>TX: RDMA Write metadata into initiator MR
    K_TGT-->>K_INIT: NVMe completions
    K_INIT-->>TX: bytes
    TX->>TX: bucket records by (key, gen). For each key: gen_current = max{gen | COMMITTED and not RELEASED and checksum OK}.<br/>Uncommitted (INTENT only) → extents freed.<br/>COMMITTED with missing / bad checksum → discarded, extents freed on next GC.<br/>COMMITTED at gen < gen_current → emit synthetic RELEASED, free extent (covers c5-crashed overwrites).<br/>Extents referenced by the max-gen COMMITTED are never reclaimed until an explicit RELEASED record is written.
    TX->>L1: initialize L1 as empty — no PENDING entries survive restart
    TX-->>CE: map ready
    CE-->>vLLM: cache online

    Note over vLLM,JBOF: === GARBAGE COLLECTION (background) ===

    TX->>TX: scan WAL, identify orphan LBA ranges (intents w/o COMMITTED, or explicit RELEASED)
    TX->>RB: release_slots(LBA_range)
    RB->>K_INIT: io_uring TRIM/UNMAP (optional)
    K_INIT->>K_TGT: NVMe Dataset Management
    K_TGT->>JBOF: block-layer deallocate
